# PINNED UNCLASSIFIED-NEW LIST -- every wire path of testing/llm-conformance/wire/*.wire.json
# that qa/field-coverage.status does not classify, RANKED: request fields, then block types (union
# arms), stream events, response fields, stream fields; shallower paths first within a tier.
#
# Surfaced 2026-10-01 when the coverage gate's path source moved from the hand-copied
# qa/field-schemas lists (412 fields) to the wire locks generated from the pinned provider specs
# (WIRE-GEN, DIALECT-SCHEMA design C stage S1). This is the #76 carry work queue: the carry lanes
# are staffed from it, top first.
#
# crates/busbar-plane-llm/tests/field_coverage.rs asserts the computed list EQUALS this file, in both
# directions and in rank order:
#
#   a path here that becomes carried/waived -> red. Delete the line in the SAME commit that lands
#                                              the coverage, so the queue shrinks visibly.
#   a path the locks gain                   -> red, because it is not listed here.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT A WAIVER LIST. A line here says "on the provider's wire, and no instrument
# watches it yet". A waiver says "not owed, and here is why" and lives in qa/field-coverage.status
# with a date and a reason. Do not move a line from here to there to make a number go green.
#
# COUNTS (dialect: request fields, block types, stream events, response fields, stream fields):
#   anthropic: 779, 239, 50, 141, 186
#   bedrock: 114, 125, 40, 487, 444
#   cohere: 33, 15, 3, 25, 72
#   gemini: 279, 0, 0, 227, 0
#   openai: 97, 24, 4, 70, 76
#   responses: 763, 543, 359, 1397, 1464

